course: dictionary
lesson: 10401
title: Context for a dinosaur word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words are names of creatures, and the sentences around them give you clues about what they are. «Triceratops had three horns and a big bony frill, weighed as much as an elephant or more, and lived at the same time and place as T. rex.» The horns, the frill and the weight all tell you this is a huge animal.
explain: Look inside the word too. Its name means «three-horned face»: tri means three, and the rest points to horns on its face. When a word is hard, check whether part of it looks like a word you already know.
explain: Then test your meaning. Swap «a large plant-eating dinosaur with three horns» into the sentence in place of the word. «A large plant-eating dinosaur with three horns had three horns and a big bony frill» sounds clumsy, but it shows you the meaning fits. A dictionary can confirm it when you are unsure.
fact: Triceratops is a noun, the name of a large plant-eating dinosaur.
fact: «Triceratops» means a large plant-eating dinosaur with three horns on its face and a big bony frill round the back of its head.
fact: Its name means «three-horned face».
fact: Triceratops was about 9 metres long, and it weighed as much as an elephant or more.
fact: The plural can be «triceratops» or «triceratopses».
exercise: «Triceratops had three horns and a big bony frill.» What is a triceratops? | A small meat-eating bird | A kind of fossil tooth | *A large plant-eating dinosaur with three horns | A tree with thick bark
exercise: «Plant-eaters were not helpless: Stegosaurus had tail spikes, Triceratops horns and a frill.» Which dinosaur in this sentence had horns? | Stegosaurus | *Triceratops | Tyrannosaurus | Ankylosaurus
exercise: One triceratops has 3 horns. How many horns do 4 triceratops have? | 7 | 3 | 4 | *12
test: Which part of a triceratops is the big bony frill? | *The shield-like bone around the back of its head | Its tail | Its feet | Its beak
test: «Triceratops was a plant-eater about 9 metres long.» How long was a triceratops, roughly? | *About 9 metres | About 9 millimetres | About 90 centimetres | About 90 metres
exam: Based on «it weighed as much as an elephant or more», what does triceratops suggest about its size? | Tiny and light | Fast and thin | *Very heavy and huge | Average, like a dog
